    "grade": "Steep Snow",
    "description": "",
    "approach": "Start at the Fourth of July trailhead above Eldora and take the trail to the Fourth of July Mine. At the mine take the right fork toward the couloir; where the trail turns east up the hillside, leave it and strike due north up the slope to the foot of the couloir that cuts the south side of South Arapahoe Peak. It begins at roughly 40 degrees and steepens toward the top, and the direct finish is s",
