    "grade": "Mod. Snow",
    "description": "",
    "approach": "Use the Skywalker Couloir approach from the Fourth of July trailhead: the trail to the Fourth of July Mine, the right fork toward the couloirs, then north across the hillside. Streetwalker is the rightmost finger of snow, about 200 yards right of Skywalker. It resembles the lower part of Skywalker, with easy to moderate snow. These are steep snow slopes in avalanche terrain, so check the avalanche",
